WEBVTT

00:01:57.994 --> 00:02:01.915
This world is teeming
with non-human beings,

00:02:01.998 --> 00:02:04.834
in the light and in the shadows.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:09.714
These beings from a nearby,
yet inaccessible realm

00:02:09.797 --> 00:02:13.843
are known as Denizens
of the Crimson World.

00:02:14.844 --> 00:02:20.892
They hide within--and
consume-people's daily lives.

00:02:20.975 --> 00:02:26.147
Yet, not a single person
is aware of their existence...

00:02:33.655 --> 00:02:39.202
"Shakugan no Shana - The Movie"

00:03:09.023 --> 00:03:11.150
"Misaki High School"

00:03:28.126 --> 00:03:29.502
Thanks!

00:03:31.713 --> 00:03:33.673
Next line, Sakai!

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:35.967
R-Right!

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:37.427
Umm...

00:03:40.013 --> 00:03:41.723
"Page 17, line 3"

00:03:43.766 --> 00:03:46.477
"My father returned from Tokyo."

00:03:52.358 --> 00:03:53.735
Sakai.

00:03:54.402 --> 00:03:55.987
Oh, Ike.

00:03:56.779 --> 00:03:58.281
Don't you have cleaning duty today?

00:03:58.364 --> 00:03:59.741
I switched with someone.

00:03:59.824 --> 00:04:01.826
I have a practice exam
at my prep school.

00:04:01.909 --> 00:04:04.871
Whoa, you're already getting
ready for college entrance exams?

00:04:04.954 --> 00:04:07.790
Yeah. I gotta keep my parents happy.

00:04:07.874 --> 00:04:10.126
It affects my allowance, y'know?

00:04:10.209 --> 00:04:11.044
--What about you?

00:04:11.044 --> 00:04:11.919
--Hmm...
--What about you?

00:04:12.003 --> 00:04:15.173
I got nothing else to do; guess I'll
check out the (IDs by the train station.

00:04:15.256 --> 00:04:16.799
"Okay, see ya!

00:04:16.799 --> 00:04:18.176
--Yeah!
--Okay, see ya!

00:04:22.138 --> 00:04:25.350
Hey! You like Sakai-kun,
don't you, Kazumi?!

00:04:25.433 --> 00:04:26.726
Huh?!

00:04:26.809 --> 00:04:27.810
H-How do you...?

00:04:27.894 --> 00:04:31.022
We've known each other
a long time! It's obvious to me!

00:04:31.105 --> 00:04:33.983
But, umm, well...

00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:35.818
Don't worry about it!

00:04:35.902 --> 00:04:39.864
If Sakai-kun is who you like,
maybe we can help each other out!

00:04:39.947 --> 00:04:41.908
Huh? Help how...?

00:04:47.372 --> 00:04:49.248
Go on, Kazumi!

00:04:51.292 --> 00:04:52.669
Oh!

00:05:00.718 --> 00:05:03.096
I guess helping each
other is out of the question.

00:05:03.179 --> 00:05:06.015
I'll just have to go it alone!

00:05:06.099 --> 00:05:08.017
All right!

00:05:12.188 --> 00:05:13.564
Hi.

00:05:17.193 --> 00:05:21.114
Umm, is Ike-kun not with you today?

00:05:21.197 --> 00:05:25.118
No. He has prep school today.
Why do you ask?

00:05:25.201 --> 00:05:28.579
Oh, no, it's just that
he's always with you.

00:05:28.663 --> 00:05:30.623
I wouldn't say "always."

00:05:30.707 --> 00:05:35.586
Anyway, I was just wondering
if Ike-kun has a girlfriend...

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:36.587
Huh?

00:05:36.671 --> 00:05:39.006
I don't think so.

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:40.466
Ah.

00:05:45.012 --> 00:05:47.640
Well, I'm gonna stop
by the station building now.

00:05:47.724 --> 00:05:50.351
Okay! See you later!

00:05:50.435 --> 00:05:53.354
I see! So she likes Ike!

00:06:04.115 --> 00:06:07.368
No, don't run so fast!

00:06:07.452 --> 00:06:09.036
Look out!

00:06:17.879 --> 00:06:20.548
No way! What them?!

00:06:23.009 --> 00:06:25.136
Wh-What's going on?!

00:06:26.137 --> 00:06:29.182
Okay! All ready!

00:06:29.265 --> 00:06:33.895
Not as many as I expected,
but it should suffice.

00:06:33.978 --> 00:06:35.104
Let us partake.

00:06:35.188 --> 00:06:37.398
Let's eat! Let's eat!

00:06:53.164 --> 00:06:55.500
Yummy, yummy!

00:06:55.583 --> 00:06:58.961
Don't talk while you're eating.
It's bad manners.

00:06:59.045 --> 00:07:00.421
Sorry!

00:07:09.931 --> 00:07:12.016
H-Hirai-san!

00:07:12.099 --> 00:07:13.226
Huh?

00:07:13.309 --> 00:07:15.978
Who is this guy?

00:07:16.062 --> 00:07:19.106
I'm not sure.
He doesn't seem to be a Denizen.

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:21.859
But he can move inside the Seal.

00:07:21.943 --> 00:07:23.778
He must be a Mystes.

00:07:23.861 --> 00:07:26.030
Oh? A Mystes?!

00:07:26.113 --> 00:07:28.324
He's one of those Torches
with a treasure inside?

00:07:28.407 --> 00:07:31.202
Yes. An especially unusual one, too.

00:07:31.285 --> 00:07:35.331
It will make a nice gift for
our master. He'll be delighted.

00:07:35.414 --> 00:07:39.210
Hooray! We did good!

00:07:41.504 --> 00:07:43.089
Gotcha!

00:07:44.632 --> 00:07:47.260
Time to eat!

00:07:59.063 --> 00:08:00.648
Who's there?!

00:08:17.248 --> 00:08:20.042
Who is she...?!

00:08:21.002 --> 00:08:22.503
Well, Alastor?

00:08:22.587 --> 00:08:25.423
Mm. They're not Denizens.

00:08:25.506 --> 00:08:27.800
Just a couple of Rinne.

00:08:27.884 --> 00:08:30.177
Her pendant can talk?!

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:33.890
How dare you cut my arm off!

00:08:34.473 --> 00:08:36.267
Now you go splat!

00:09:07.131 --> 00:09:08.549
Don't!

00:09:18.059 --> 00:09:20.186
Looks like it was just a shell.

00:09:20.269 --> 00:09:22.897
Its real body managed to escape...

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:25.608
It could still be nearby.

00:09:28.235 --> 00:09:29.779
--I take it this is a Mystes.

00:09:29.779 --> 00:09:30.821
--Mm.
--I take it this is a Mystes.

00:09:30.905 --> 00:09:34.241
A somewhat peculiar one, at that.

00:09:34.325 --> 00:09:35.701
What?

00:09:38.913 --> 00:09:40.289
Why...?!

00:09:43.668 --> 00:09:45.002
I've been cut?

00:09:45.086 --> 00:09:46.879
I've been cut...

00:09:49.048 --> 00:09:50.841
Flame-haired and burning-eyed...

00:09:50.925 --> 00:09:54.887
You must be the Flame Haze
of Alastor, Flame of the Heavens...

00:09:54.971 --> 00:09:57.098
You accursed Tool
for Destruction Attack!

00:09:57.181 --> 00:09:59.642
That's right. What of it?

00:09:59.725 --> 00:10:02.520
My master won't stand for this!

00:10:02.603 --> 00:10:03.604
That's right.

00:10:03.688 --> 00:10:07.024
Very soon he'll be
screaming his death throes.

00:10:07.108 --> 00:10:08.401
You little...!

00:10:08.484 --> 00:10:12.321
But right now it's your turn to scream!

00:10:24.583 --> 00:10:26.377
So that's its real body!

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:28.045
Behind you!

00:10:47.231 --> 00:10:48.899
It got away.

00:10:48.983 --> 00:10:52.611
From the way it talked, it must have
some pretty heavy-duty support...

00:10:52.695 --> 00:10:56.907
We may be able to destroy
our first Crimson Lord in a while.

00:10:56.991 --> 00:10:58.242
Still...

00:10:58.325 --> 00:11:01.078
H-Help! It hurts!

00:11:01.162 --> 00:11:02.955
Please, call an ambulance...!

00:11:03.039 --> 00:11:03.998
Urgh!

00:11:04.081 --> 00:11:05.666
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:08.044
$0 you got cut! Big deal!

00:11:08.127 --> 00:11:09.128
You can't be serious...!

00:11:09.211 --> 00:11:11.839
You're but a vessel of your former life!

00:11:11.922 --> 00:11:15.134
If you were human, such a grave
injury would have meant instant death.

00:11:15.217 --> 00:11:17.094
If I were human...?!

00:11:17.178 --> 00:11:21.682
I have to stop it! I have
to stop the bleeding before-l

00:11:21.766 --> 00:11:24.602
I'm not bleeding...? What's going on?!

00:11:24.685 --> 00:11:26.854
I must be dreaming!

00:11:40.076 --> 00:11:42.119
I'm on fire! I'm on fire!

00:11:42.203 --> 00:11:43.788
Huh? How...?!

00:11:43.871 --> 00:11:45.247
Now, then.

00:11:59.762 --> 00:12:01.222
Hirai-san!

00:12:05.726 --> 00:12:08.395
Thank goodness!
She's back to normal...

00:12:08.479 --> 00:12:10.564
That does it for the Torches.

00:12:10.648 --> 00:12:12.483
I'll have to use a couple to fix things now.

00:12:12.566 --> 00:12:15.611
Mm. They certainly gorged themselves.

00:12:15.694 --> 00:12:19.031
Their master must be quite the glutton.

00:12:32.336 --> 00:12:33.921
All done.

00:12:42.471 --> 00:12:47.476
Doesn't anyone realize
what just happened?

00:12:48.686 --> 00:12:51.730
Hirai-san! Wait, Hirai-san!

00:12:51.814 --> 00:12:54.024
What the...?

00:12:54.108 --> 00:12:55.693
What is that?

00:12:56.777 --> 00:12:58.362
Hirai-san...

00:13:13.502 --> 00:13:14.712
No...

00:13:14.795 --> 00:13:16.172
Why?!

00:13:17.464 --> 00:13:18.257
It couldn't be!

00:13:18.340 --> 00:13:20.384
Hey! Wait up!

00:13:20.467 --> 00:13:22.553
What was that just now?!

00:13:22.636 --> 00:13:25.097
Where did that kid go?!

00:13:25.181 --> 00:13:27.641
And what's the fire
thing I see inside them--?!

00:13:27.725 --> 00:13:29.393
Urgh, this thing's bugging me!

00:13:29.476 --> 00:13:32.396
Can I please extinguish this one, Alastor?

00:13:32.479 --> 00:13:35.691
No. We mustn't open a Mystes carelessly.

00:13:35.774 --> 00:13:38.569
I know, but it's just so annoying!

00:13:38.652 --> 00:13:42.907
Simply tell it the truth.
That should quiet it.

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:47.453
Why do you keep calling me an "it"?!

00:13:47.536 --> 00:13:51.415
That's just it. You're not
a person" you're a thing.

00:14:03.594 --> 00:14:08.724
Those monsters were Rinne,
minions of Crimson Denizens.

00:14:08.807 --> 00:14:14.104
They appear throughout the
world and consume people's existences.

00:14:14.188 --> 00:14:20.444
Those whose existences are
eaten cease to have ever existed.

00:14:20.527 --> 00:14:25.366
The world's balance would be disrupted
if people suddenly disappeared,

00:14:25.449 --> 00:14:27.117
so we leave Torches in their place.

00:14:27.201 --> 00:14:28.285
Torches?

00:14:28.369 --> 00:14:32.206
The leftover scum of
those who disappear. Like you.

00:14:32.289 --> 00:14:37.044
The real you is long dead.
His existence was eaten.

00:14:37.127 --> 00:14:39.255
That's crazy...

00:14:41.215 --> 00:14:43.634
You can see your own flame, can't you?

00:14:43.717 --> 00:14:45.094
Huh?

00:14:59.984 --> 00:15:01.735
It's not just you.

00:15:01.819 --> 00:15:05.447
Everyone you see with
a flame inside them is a Torch;

00:15:05.531 --> 00:15:09.827
the leftover scum of someone
whose existence was eaten.

00:15:09.910 --> 00:15:12.663
But they're only meant
to soften the impact;

00:15:12.746 --> 00:15:15.916
the flames will grow smaller
and eventually go out entirely.

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:17.251
They'll vanish?!

00:15:17.334 --> 00:15:19.878
Yes. They'll burn out.

00:15:24.508 --> 00:15:26.552
That's it for the explanation!

00:15:26.635 --> 00:15:29.722
I'm... already dead...

00:15:37.604 --> 00:15:39.857
How long are you going to follow me?

00:15:39.940 --> 00:15:42.276
My house is this way...

00:15:42.359 --> 00:15:43.736
Oh.

00:15:51.785 --> 00:15:54.246
I'm already dead...

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:57.624
No, it's Yuji Sakai who's dead.

00:15:57.708 --> 00:15:59.168
I'm just...

00:16:00.294 --> 00:16:02.963
No, this is too hard to accept!

00:16:04.548 --> 00:16:06.342
Say...

00:16:06.425 --> 00:16:07.801
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

00:16:07.885 --> 00:16:09.303
Why do you keep bugging me?!

00:16:09.386 --> 00:16:11.722
Just what are you? Human?!

00:16:11.805 --> 00:16:13.515
I'm a Flame Haze!

00:16:13.599 --> 00:16:15.351
Fla...? What?

00:16:15.434 --> 00:16:16.685
A Flame Haze.

00:16:16.769 --> 00:16:21.273
One who hunts and destroys
existence-eating Crimson Denizens.

00:16:21.357 --> 00:16:25.611
The Torches we leave behind only
serve to cover up what has transpired.

00:16:25.694 --> 00:16:28.238
They do nothing to alleviate the
danger facing this world:

00:16:28.322 --> 00:16:31.283
the indiscriminate theft of existences.

00:16:35.454 --> 00:16:37.331
Flame Haze...

00:16:39.375 --> 00:16:41.960
Please forgive me, Master.

00:16:42.044 --> 00:16:46.465
I lost one of your favorite Rinne...

00:16:46.548 --> 00:16:50.260
You aren't to blame, Marianne.

00:16:50.344 --> 00:16:54.431
You ran into a somewhat
troublesome Flame Haze, that's all.

00:16:54.515 --> 00:16:59.978
If anything, you deserve
praise for finding a Mystes.

00:17:00.062 --> 00:17:02.689
But I let it get away.

00:17:02.773 --> 00:17:07.403
Please, let me hunt it for you!

00:17:07.486 --> 00:17:10.823
That sentiment pleases me, Marianne.

00:17:10.906 --> 00:17:14.410
But we needn't be hasty.

00:17:14.493 --> 00:17:17.579
We must think--and act--with care.

00:17:17.663 --> 00:17:21.291
We're dealing with the Flame of the
Heavens' Flame Haze, after all.

00:17:21.375 --> 00:17:22.751
Yes.

00:17:30.884 --> 00:17:34.430
Take a look at the
Crystal Altar, Marianne.

00:17:37.724 --> 00:17:40.644
How beautiful it is...

00:17:40.727 --> 00:17:46.275
Let us forget about the Flame Haze
for now and savor this moment...

00:17:55.659 --> 00:17:58.829
Yu-chan! Breakfast is ready!

00:17:58.912 --> 00:18:00.706
Be right there...

00:18:05.919 --> 00:18:10.007
It's unusual for you to
oversleep, Yu-chan.

00:18:10.090 --> 00:18:13.343
You came home last night
and went straight to bed.

00:18:13.427 --> 00:18:14.970
Are you sick?

00:18:15.053 --> 00:18:17.181
No, I'm fine.

00:18:21.518 --> 00:18:26.023
Today we take a look at
the sand-stormy Gobi Desert!

00:18:26.106 --> 00:18:28.609
Oh, the Gobi Desert!

00:18:28.692 --> 00:18:32.863
That's where your father is!
Maybe we'll see him!

00:18:32.946 --> 00:18:34.323
Oh...

00:18:39.077 --> 00:18:44.416
Good, Mom's okay. She isn't a Torch.

00:18:44.500 --> 00:18:46.835
If she found out
I'm already dead, she'd...

00:18:46.919 --> 00:18:51.757
Oh, but soon she'll
never have had me, huh?

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:55.761
I guess never having existed
is better than causing her grief...

00:18:59.473 --> 00:19:03.894
Err, right, the real Yuji Sakai
doesn't exist anymore.

00:19:06.188 --> 00:19:09.441
Yu-chan? ls something wrong?

00:19:09.525 --> 00:19:11.443
Oh, no, it's nothing.

00:19:11.527 --> 00:19:15.572
I better get going. My new
teacher is really strict about time.

00:19:15.656 --> 00:19:16.740
I'll see you later.

00:19:16.823 --> 00:19:19.535
Take care! Have a good day!

00:19:19.618 --> 00:19:23.539
So what is this I'm worried about now?

00:19:23.622 --> 00:19:29.920
The real Yuji Sakai would naturally
feel hopeless and anxious,

00:19:30.003 --> 00:19:31.672
but I feel...

00:19:36.927 --> 00:19:38.428
What are you doing here?

00:19:38.512 --> 00:19:40.597
I figured keeping an eye on you

00:19:40.681 --> 00:19:44.059
would be faster than trying
to find Crimson Denizens.

00:19:44.142 --> 00:19:49.064
You're a rather rare Torch.
I'm sure you'll attract more.

00:19:50.691 --> 00:19:52.067
Oh...

00:19:54.903 --> 00:19:59.783
Come to think of it, those Rinne
things yesterday called me a "Mystes"...

00:19:59.866 --> 00:20:02.911
Oh? I'm impressed you remember.

00:20:02.995 --> 00:20:09.167
A Mystes is a Torch containing a
Denizen-made Treasure or unique power.

00:20:09.251 --> 00:20:10.460
Treasure?

00:20:10.544 --> 00:20:17.551
A rare item that moves between
random Torches each time one burns out.

00:20:17.634 --> 00:20:20.178
It's like a traveling
treasure vault of sorts.

00:20:20.262 --> 00:20:21.680
Why me...?

00:20:21.763 --> 00:20:26.059
I wouldn't know.
Treasures move as they see fit.

00:20:26.143 --> 00:20:31.565
The enemy will likely
strike just before you burn out.

00:20:31.648 --> 00:20:33.609
Before I burn out...

00:20:34.901 --> 00:20:37.779
Tell me, what exactly am I?

00:20:37.863 --> 00:20:39.948
A Torch and a Mystes.

00:20:40.032 --> 00:20:43.535
But all my thoughts are
things Yuji Sakai would think about!

00:20:43.619 --> 00:20:45.996
Of course they are.
You're his leftover scum.

00:20:47.581 --> 00:20:48.999
Oh...

00:20:49.082 --> 00:20:50.459
Still...

00:20:57.257 --> 00:20:59.885
...there are too many Torches in this city.

00:20:59.968 --> 00:21:03.472
Mm. Something is
unquestionably amiss.

00:21:04.181 --> 00:21:06.391
What does that mean?

00:21:09.144 --> 00:21:10.520
Hirai-san!

00:21:12.606 --> 00:21:14.733
Her flame is small...

00:21:14.816 --> 00:21:16.735
It's almost gone.

00:21:16.818 --> 00:21:19.196
But the attack was only yesterday!

00:21:19.279 --> 00:21:21.281
Then most of its flame was eaten.

00:21:21.365 --> 00:21:24.284
Yesterday's Rinne did
gorge themselves and all.

00:21:25.786 --> 00:21:28.080
Hirai-san! Hirai-san!

00:21:28.163 --> 00:21:29.706
Good morning!

00:21:29.790 --> 00:21:31.667
Umm... Good morning.

00:21:32.626 --> 00:21:34.544
Good morning...

00:21:34.628 --> 00:21:36.004
This...

00:21:37.381 --> 00:21:39.508
...is the same Hirai-san?

00:21:41.259 --> 00:21:43.595
She has to the end of the day, at best.

00:21:43.679 --> 00:21:46.223
You can't be serious!
Isn't there anything we can do?!

00:21:46.306 --> 00:21:49.101
No. That's just the leftover scum.

00:21:49.184 --> 00:21:51.520
The real her is dead.

00:21:53.814 --> 00:21:55.565
That's...

00:21:55.649 --> 00:21:57.234
That's horrible!

00:21:58.694 --> 00:22:01.405
Hirai-san! We're gonna
be late! Let's run!

00:22:01.488 --> 00:22:04.157
Come on! Cheer up!

00:22:05.409 --> 00:22:06.702
What's with that one?

00:22:06.785 --> 00:22:09.788
It didn't even ask for itself to be fixed...

00:22:09.871 --> 00:22:14.626
It most likely fully grasped the situation
once placed in another's shoes.

00:22:14.710 --> 00:22:15.752
Hmph

00:22:15.836 --> 00:22:18.088
Hirai-san disappearing...

00:22:18.171 --> 00:22:20.173
I refuse to accept it!

00:22:20.257 --> 00:22:23.218
I was wondering if
Ike-kun has a girlfriend...

00:22:31.017 --> 00:22:32.602
Hey!

00:22:32.686 --> 00:22:37.107
You're stupendously late, Sakai!

00:22:37.190 --> 00:22:38.775
--I'm sorry.
--One demerit for Sakai...

00:22:40.110 --> 00:22:42.654
Umm, what about Hirai-san?

00:22:42.738 --> 00:22:45.198
Oh, right. I didn't see her there.

00:22:45.282 --> 00:22:48.243
Whatever. Just take your seats.

00:22:50.454 --> 00:22:52.622
What's goin' on? This isn't like you!

00:22:52.706 --> 00:22:54.082
Mm.

00:22:59.796 --> 00:23:02.758
No one's paying her any attention...

00:23:07.929 --> 00:23:09.264
"Grade 10, Class 2"

00:23:09.765 --> 00:23:11.808
Hirai-san! What are you doing for lunch?

00:23:11.892 --> 00:23:14.478
Huh? Nothing...

00:23:14.561 --> 00:23:16.688
--You don't mind, do you, Ike?!

00:23:16.688 --> 00:23:17.647
--No, not really...
--You don't mind, do you, Ike?!

00:23:17.731 --> 00:23:19.107
Okay?

00:23:27.073 --> 00:23:29.993
So it turns out this teacher
at my new prep school

00:23:30.076 --> 00:23:33.038
is actually Murata's older brother!

00:23:33.121 --> 00:23:35.832
Say, Ike. Do you
have prep school today?

00:23:35.916 --> 00:23:37.167
No, I got today off.

00:23:37.250 --> 00:23:40.837
Oh, then we should hang
out by the station after school!

00:23:40.921 --> 00:23:43.799
Along with Hirai-san!
You don't have any plans, right?

00:23:43.882 --> 00:23:45.759
Huh? I guess that's okay...

00:23:45.842 --> 00:23:46.885
Okay! It's decided!

00:23:46.968 --> 00:23:49.930
Hirai-san! Ike says he'll come!

00:23:56.311 --> 00:23:58.021
Come on, Ike! Scoot in more!

00:23:58.104 --> 00:24:01.149
Here goes!

00:24:01.233 --> 00:24:03.360
That looks pretty good!

00:24:03.443 --> 00:24:06.238
Oh, I got kinda in the way...

00:24:06.321 --> 00:24:07.906
Sorry, Hirai-san.

00:24:07.989 --> 00:24:09.699
Hey, listen...

00:24:09.783 --> 00:24:12.160
What's next?
A prize-catcher game?

00:24:12.244 --> 00:24:15.497
Hirai-san! Why don't
you play a game against Ike?

00:24:18.166 --> 00:24:20.544
Oh, Ike. Hang out
with Hirai-san for a minute.

00:24:20.627 --> 00:24:21.920
I'll be right back.

00:24:22.003 --> 00:24:23.880
Hey! Sakai!

00:24:44.401 --> 00:24:47.070
Stay still, will you?!
You're supposed to be bait!

00:24:47.153 --> 00:24:50.073
I know you sympathize with it,
but it's only a Torch!

00:24:50.156 --> 00:24:51.783
You can't stop it from going out.

00:24:51.867 --> 00:24:55.161
But if I can keep
people from forgetting her...!

00:24:55.245 --> 00:24:56.329
--It's pointless.

00:24:56.329 --> 00:24:57.914
--Even so...!
--It's pointless.

00:25:02.168 --> 00:25:05.922
I've never met such
a stupid Torch in my life.

00:25:06.006 --> 00:25:07.173
Mm.

00:25:08.008 --> 00:25:09.926
Huh? Ike, where's Hirai-san?

00:25:10.010 --> 00:25:12.512
Huh? Hirai who?

00:25:12.596 --> 00:25:14.973
You know, Hirai-san!
You were just with her!

00:25:15.056 --> 00:25:16.683
I was?

00:25:16.766 --> 00:25:18.393
What do you mean, "I was?"

00:25:18.476 --> 00:25:20.979
Don't tell me she's already...

00:25:21.062 --> 00:25:24.441
Oh, yeah. I think she left
a minute ago or something.

00:25:24.524 --> 00:25:26.610
Really?! You're sure?!

00:25:26.693 --> 00:25:27.235
Yeah, I think.

00:25:27.277 --> 00:25:29.779
Oh, did I beat this stage?!

00:25:29.863 --> 00:25:32.824
Ike! Why don't you seem to care?!

00:25:32.908 --> 00:25:34.242
Think back!

00:25:34.326 --> 00:25:37.329
The three of us
were together a minute ago!

00:25:37.412 --> 00:25:40.415
And Hirai-san, she... she...!

00:25:40.498 --> 00:25:43.293
I was wondering if Ike-kun has a girlfriend...

00:25:45.378 --> 00:25:49.174
Man, what's gotten into you,
Sakai? Are you okay?

00:25:49.257 --> 00:25:50.926
It isn't Ike's fault.

00:25:51.009 --> 00:25:53.386
This is what it means to be a Torch...

00:25:55.472 --> 00:25:57.599
What's his deal?

00:25:59.559 --> 00:26:02.437
Hirai-san... Please tell
me you haven't vanished yet!

00:26:02.437 --> 00:26:11.613
<i>As the glow of the sunset sky
dyes the city and your profile</i>

00:26:13.615 --> 00:26:24.626
<i>what are you thinking,
watching, and feeling?</i>

00:26:24.626 --> 00:26:28.088
What a relief.
So this is where you went.

00:26:28.088 --> 00:26:34.219
<i>Even if we can't see our
future further down the road,</i>

00:26:34.219 --> 00:26:38.390
That way you'll have a
photo of you and Ike together.

00:26:38.390 --> 00:26:40.517
<i>I will hold your hand</i>

00:26:40.600 --> 00:26:46.606
<i>and race to the ends of the earth</i>

00:26:48.108 --> 00:26:49.567
Hmm? What?

00:26:49.567 --> 00:26:54.280
<i>All the tears, lies,
sadness, and regrets</i>

00:26:54.280 --> 00:26:56.074
Ah, so that's why you came here.

00:26:56.074 --> 00:26:59.911
<i>Are proof that
I was here with you</i>

00:26:59.911 --> 00:27:01.079
Hirai-san.

00:27:01.079 --> 00:27:09.546
<i>I believe "goodbye" is the beginning
of memories only couples can have</i>

00:27:09.629 --> 00:27:13.591
<i>So I swear upon my heart</i>

00:27:13.675 --> 00:27:23.018
<i>that someday, again...!</i>

00:27:30.608 --> 00:27:32.652
Hirai-san...

00:27:32.736 --> 00:27:35.030
Now do you understand?

00:27:35.030 --> 00:27:41.828
<i>Now let's call forth our smiles,
dreams, love, and joy</i>

00:27:41.911 --> 00:27:44.706
<i>and let it resound forever</i>

00:27:44.706 --> 00:27:47.208
Leftover scum will eventually burn out.

00:27:47.208 --> 00:27:54.382
<i>Because I refuse to
believe that tangible things</i>

00:27:54.382 --> 00:27:55.050
<i>You're wrong'.</i>

00:27:55.050 --> 00:28:03.641
<i>Is all that exists here</i>

00:28:03.641 --> 00:28:04.059
That she was Yukari Hirai!

00:28:04.142 --> 00:28:07.228
There's no question
she existed! Right here!

00:28:09.856 --> 00:28:11.316
She existed...

00:28:11.399 --> 00:28:12.609
SQ?

00:28:12.692 --> 00:28:14.611
I exist here, too.

00:28:14.694 --> 00:28:18.698
<i>I know</i> I'm Yuji Sakai.

00:28:18.782 --> 00:28:21.034
You're just a Torch.

00:28:21.117 --> 00:28:23.078
But I'm still Yuji Sakai.

00:28:23.161 --> 00:28:24.579
And you're...

00:28:24.662 --> 00:28:27.832
I'm just a Flame Haze. That's all.

00:28:27.916 --> 00:28:29.959
In a sense, I'm no
different from a Torch.

00:28:30.043 --> 00:28:32.545
Stop saying "just"!

00:28:32.629 --> 00:28:34.172
But it's the truth.

00:28:34.255 --> 00:28:38.093
You're just a Torch,
and I'm just a Flame Haze.

00:28:38.176 --> 00:28:39.135
<i>--You're wrong'.</i>

00:28:39.135 --> 00:28:40.303
--I'm not!
--You're wrong!

00:28:40.386 --> 00:28:42.347
Why are You so...?!

00:28:48.645 --> 00:28:49.479
What?

00:28:49.562 --> 00:28:50.772
--Your name...

00:28:50.772 --> 00:28:51.272
--Huh?
--Your name...

00:28:51.314 --> 00:28:53.274
Tell me your name.

00:28:54.651 --> 00:28:58.238
I don't have a name.
I'm just a Flame Haze.

00:28:58.321 --> 00:28:59.614
There you go again...

00:28:59.697 --> 00:29:01.616
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

00:29:01.699 --> 00:29:03.284
I don't need a name!

00:29:03.368 --> 00:29:05.745
When I need to distinguish
myself from other Flame Hazes,

00:29:05.829 --> 00:29:08.456
I go by "the Flame Haze
with Nietono no Shana"!

00:29:08.540 --> 00:29:10.166
Nietono no Shana...?

00:29:10.250 --> 00:29:13.294
It's the name of the sword she wields.

00:29:13.378 --> 00:29:15.213
Nietono no Shana...

00:29:16.089 --> 00:29:20.135
Then from now on, I'll call you "Shana"!

00:29:20.218 --> 00:29:23.513
You're Shana! You're not
just a Flame Haze anymore!

00:29:23.596 --> 00:29:27.058
And I'm not just a Torch!
I'm Yuji Sakai!

00:29:33.189 --> 00:29:35.817
Don't give me names I don't want.

00:30:19.444 --> 00:30:21.738
Kazumi! Your bath's ready!

00:30:21.821 --> 00:30:23.198
Okay!

00:30:36.044 --> 00:30:39.714
I'll give them to Sakai-kun tomorrow.

00:30:39.797 --> 00:30:43.051
But would that put him off?
Giving them without a real reason...

00:30:45.178 --> 00:30:48.139
I guess I'll ask Yukari-chan first...

00:31:02.779 --> 00:31:05.198
What's the matter, Sakai?

00:31:05.281 --> 00:31:07.075
Ike. Is that...?

00:31:08.743 --> 00:31:11.454
Huh? What about Hirai-san now?

00:31:11.537 --> 00:31:13.665
Hirai-san? Her?

00:31:13.748 --> 00:31:16.376
Ike, let me see your homework answers!

00:31:16.459 --> 00:31:17.710
Sure.

00:31:17.794 --> 00:31:21.047
You should splash your face
with cold water or something.

00:31:23.299 --> 00:31:24.509
What are you doing?

00:31:24.592 --> 00:31:28.263
I told you. I'm keeping an eye on you.

00:31:28.346 --> 00:31:30.598
But I didn't think you meant like this.

00:31:30.682 --> 00:31:33.601
Besides, that's Hirai-san's seat.

00:31:33.685 --> 00:31:36.646
I am Yukari Hirai.

00:31:36.729 --> 00:31:41.276
I've inserted myself
into Yukari Hirai's existence.

00:31:41.359 --> 00:31:43.987
L-inserted...?

00:31:44.070 --> 00:31:46.698
Using her leftover scum from yesterday.

00:31:48.700 --> 00:31:50.702
But you look nothing like her.

00:31:50.785 --> 00:31:52.453
Yukari-chan!

00:31:52.537 --> 00:31:53.663
Good morning!

00:31:53.746 --> 00:31:56.666
Sakai-kun... Good morning!

00:31:56.749 --> 00:31:58.543
Good morning...

00:32:02.255 --> 00:32:03.172
I said it!

00:32:03.256 --> 00:32:06.384
Yoshida-san used to be
good friends with Hirai-san,

00:32:06.467 --> 00:32:07.719
but she didn't notice at all...

00:32:07.802 --> 00:32:10.763
When you insert yourself
into someone's existence,

00:32:10.847 --> 00:32:13.266
it's not about trying
to resemble that person.

00:32:13.349 --> 00:32:16.185
I've taken Yukari Hirai's existence,
as acknowledged by others,

00:32:16.269 --> 00:32:17.812
and replaced it with me.

00:32:17.895 --> 00:32:20.481
You can't be serious...

00:32:20.565 --> 00:32:24.027
Hirai-san! Thanks for lending
me your notebook the other day!

00:32:24.110 --> 00:32:25.486
Mm.

00:32:30.533 --> 00:32:32.201
No...

00:32:32.285 --> 00:32:35.538
I know who Yukari Hirai was!

00:32:36.956 --> 00:32:39.167
Good morning, Shana!

00:32:49.469 --> 00:32:53.723
The Flame Haze appears
to be sticking with the Mystes.

00:32:53.806 --> 00:32:54.640
Yes.

00:32:54.724 --> 00:32:57.560
She must be waiting for us to strike.

00:32:57.643 --> 00:33:01.022
A sound assessment. Very sound.

00:33:02.940 --> 00:33:06.778
Perhaps we should
comply and pay a little visit.

00:33:06.861 --> 00:33:10.448
I'll admit, I am intrigued by
the Treasure inside the Mystes.

00:33:10.531 --> 00:33:13.451
Then please send me.

00:33:13.534 --> 00:33:17.205
I want to make up
for my failure the other day.

00:33:17.288 --> 00:33:18.664
Very well.

00:33:19.415 --> 00:33:22.877
But this is "Flame-haired
Burning-eyed" we're dealing with.

00:33:24.921 --> 00:33:26.881
Take this with you.

00:33:39.018 --> 00:33:41.062
Do not leave my side.

00:33:41.145 --> 00:33:42.772
I can do what I want.

00:33:42.855 --> 00:33:46.401
Yukari-chan. Could you
walk home with me today?

00:33:46.484 --> 00:33:47.860
--I'd like your advice about--

00:33:47.860 --> 00:33:49.821
--No. I'm busy.
--I'd like your advice about--

00:33:51.114 --> 00:33:52.281
O-Oh.

00:33:52.365 --> 00:33:53.741
Sorry.

00:33:56.119 --> 00:34:00.540
Yukari-chan seems kind of scary today...

00:34:00.623 --> 00:34:01.290
“Shana!

00:34:01.290 --> 00:34:02.166
--Sakai.
“Shana!

00:34:02.250 --> 00:34:04.919
Could we stop by the
bookstore on the way home?

00:34:05.002 --> 00:34:06.379
Sure.

00:34:07.713 --> 00:34:08.798
One's here!

00:34:14.095 --> 00:34:15.847
This is just like before!

00:34:15.930 --> 00:34:17.014
It's a Seal.

00:34:17.098 --> 00:34:18.933
Wait! At school?!

00:34:19.016 --> 00:34:23.354
The location doesn't matter,
just as long as you're there.

00:34:23.438 --> 00:34:25.690
I saw this coming a mile away!

00:34:31.654 --> 00:34:32.905
Wait! Everyone's still here!

00:34:32.989 --> 00:34:36.367
The enemy laid this Seal.
Talk to them, not me.

00:34:41.581 --> 00:34:43.958
Everyone's gonna
get caught in the fighting!

00:34:44.041 --> 00:34:48.129
I hafta do something!
This is all my fault!

00:34:48.212 --> 00:34:49.589
Sorry!

00:34:56.137 --> 00:34:57.513
Ike!

00:35:20.661 --> 00:35:22.455
Cheap tricks!

00:35:42.975 --> 00:35:44.352
Ike!

00:35:50.900 --> 00:35:51.859
Yoshida-san!

00:35:52.276 --> 00:35:53.236
Yoshida-san!

00:35:53.945 --> 00:35:55.321
Yoshida-san!

00:35:59.242 --> 00:36:01.285
You're that Rinne from the other day.

00:36:01.369 --> 00:36:03.120
What is your master's name?

00:36:03.204 --> 00:36:06.832
Do you... honestly think... I'll tell you?

00:36:06.916 --> 00:36:09.752
No, just making sure.

00:36:09.835 --> 00:36:13.214
But from the way he wastes
his measly little pawns like this,

00:36:13.297 --> 00:36:15.925
he's gotta be one big idiot.

00:36:16.008 --> 00:36:17.593
Why, you...!

00:36:29.772 --> 00:36:31.899
Hello, little one.

00:36:33.317 --> 00:36:35.736
At last we meet.

00:36:35.820 --> 00:36:38.489
<i>This</i> is a Crimson Denizen. I can tell...

00:36:40.825 --> 00:36:41.867
Remarkable.

00:36:41.951 --> 00:36:44.787
With a single sword,
you've managed to overwhelm

00:36:44.870 --> 00:36:48.583
my adored "Regular Sharp" Treasure.

00:36:48.666 --> 00:36:52.128
Please forgive me, Master...

00:36:52.211 --> 00:36:54.922
No, I'm the one who should apologize

00:36:55.006 --> 00:36:57.967
for giving you a Treasure
you're unaccustomed to using.

00:36:59.427 --> 00:37:02.638
Honestly, Flame Hazes are just terrible.

00:37:02.722 --> 00:37:04.265
Are you the master?

00:37:04.348 --> 00:37:08.894
Yes. Hunter Friagne. That is my name.

00:37:08.978 --> 00:37:11.022
This is my first time meeting you in person...

00:37:11.105 --> 00:37:13.608
...Alastor, Flame of the Heavens.

00:37:13.691 --> 00:37:15.610
Do not be deceived by appearances.

00:37:15.693 --> 00:37:20.615
He is a powerful Crimson Lord
who has used his numerous Treasures

00:37:20.698 --> 00:37:22.283
to slay many Flame Hazes.

00:37:22.366 --> 00:37:23.659
Yeah.

00:37:23.743 --> 00:37:25.953
So she's your contractor...

00:37:26.037 --> 00:37:28.998
A flame-haired and
burning-eyed slayer, huh?

00:37:29.081 --> 00:37:31.751
Honestly, I'm a bit disappointed...

00:37:31.834 --> 00:37:33.127
What?!

00:37:33.210 --> 00:37:34.670
Flame of the Heavens.

00:37:34.754 --> 00:37:39.091
Your power as a great
Crimson God is wasted

00:37:39.175 --> 00:37:42.303
with such a feeble contractor.

00:37:42.386 --> 00:37:45.640
Want to find out for yourself?!

00:37:45.723 --> 00:37:49.977
Countless slayers have said that
just before meeting defeat by my hand.

00:37:50.061 --> 00:37:52.897
I can't risk harming the Mystes, however.

00:37:52.980 --> 00:37:54.315
We will meet again.

00:37:54.398 --> 00:37:57.068
These are my hunting grounds, after all.

00:37:57.151 --> 00:38:01.405
I look forward to
seeing what's inside you.

00:38:08.120 --> 00:38:11.415
It was no ordinary Denizen, after all.

00:38:16.504 --> 00:38:20.257
A Crimson Lord,
and Hunter Friagne, at that...

00:38:20.341 --> 00:38:22.843
It's no surprise he's after the Mystes.

00:38:22.927 --> 00:38:25.012
He said these were
his "hunting grounds."

00:38:25.096 --> 00:38:28.265
He must be why there are
so many Torches in this city.

00:38:28.349 --> 00:38:31.686
Mm. That would explain it.

00:38:31.769 --> 00:38:34.313
He's horrific...

00:38:34.397 --> 00:38:38.109
I have to fix things here.
Move, so I can use her.

00:38:38.192 --> 00:38:39.735
Huh? Use...?!

00:38:39.819 --> 00:38:43.906
I'm going to use her power of
existence to fix what's been broken.

00:38:44.949 --> 00:38:46.867
You're going to use Yoshida-san?!

00:38:46.951 --> 00:38:47.702
That's right.

00:38:47.743 --> 00:38:50.705
They didn't leave any
uneaten Torches behind,

00:38:50.788 --> 00:38:53.124
so she's the only natural choice.

00:38:53.207 --> 00:38:56.377
A single human on the verge
of death is more than enough.

00:38:56.460 --> 00:39:00.214
And if I replace her with a Torch,
everything will be fine and dandy again.

00:39:00.297 --> 00:39:04.051
The heck it will!
She'll be dead, just like me!

00:39:04.135 --> 00:39:09.056
There's no other way. I need
<i>some</i> source of energy to fix this.

00:39:09.140 --> 00:39:11.934
It doesn't have to be her, though.
I could use him.

00:39:13.978 --> 00:39:17.106
No, that's not fair...

00:39:17.189 --> 00:39:19.066
Then shall I use you?

00:39:19.150 --> 00:39:20.526
Huh?

00:39:24.029 --> 00:39:25.281
I'll accept that.

00:39:25.364 --> 00:39:30.911
Wow, that was a simple decision
after your hissy fit just now.

00:39:30.995 --> 00:39:32.163
It wasn't simple.

00:39:32.246 --> 00:39:36.292
Then why would you throw
away the time you have left?

00:39:36.375 --> 00:39:38.085
I'm not throwing it away.

00:39:38.169 --> 00:39:40.129
I'm putting it to use!

00:39:42.423 --> 00:39:43.924
What a strange--

00:39:44.008 --> 00:39:45.468
No, weird--

00:39:45.551 --> 00:39:46.927
No, disgusting...

00:39:47.011 --> 00:39:49.263
Yes! What a disgusting guy!

00:39:49.346 --> 00:39:51.807
You certainly used up a lot of his power.

00:39:51.891 --> 00:39:56.187
It's not my fault.
It was his suggestion.

00:39:56.270 --> 00:39:58.939
He's lucky I didn't use it all up.

00:40:02.318 --> 00:40:03.861
I thought you'd be up here.

00:40:03.944 --> 00:40:05.321
Something wrong with that?

00:40:05.404 --> 00:40:07.156
I never said that.

00:40:07.239 --> 00:40:09.825
How did you know we were here?

00:40:09.909 --> 00:40:13.454
I just somehow felt
like you were, I guess.

00:40:13.537 --> 00:40:14.955
I see.

00:40:15.039 --> 00:40:17.541
After coming in contact with such power,

00:40:17.625 --> 00:40:19.460
it's only natural you
would begin to sense it.

00:40:19.543 --> 00:40:20.377
What do you want?

00:40:20.461 --> 00:40:25.508
Well, it's just, I can't exactly relax
knowing there's a girl on my roof.

00:40:25.591 --> 00:40:27.259
Why don't you come inside?

00:40:27.343 --> 00:40:28.344
Inside?

00:40:28.427 --> 00:40:30.262
You'll get soaked out here.

00:40:30.346 --> 00:40:34.558
Besides, if you wanna keep an eye
on me, shouldn't you stay close by?

00:40:34.642 --> 00:40:36.143
Good point...

00:40:36.227 --> 00:40:38.395
That never crossed your mind?

00:40:38.479 --> 00:40:40.981
Does that give you
the right to act so arrogant?

00:40:41.065 --> 00:40:43.025
I'm not being arrogant...

00:40:44.985 --> 00:40:45.986
I'm going in.

00:40:46.070 --> 00:40:49.406
Uhh, err, okay. Make yourself at home.

00:40:52.326 --> 00:40:55.913
You can have the bed.
I'll sleep in my dad's study.

00:40:55.996 --> 00:40:59.875
I came in to keep an eye on you.
Why would we sleep in separate rooms?

00:40:59.959 --> 00:41:01.836
Huh? But...

00:41:01.919 --> 00:41:04.880
This was your suggestion.
You will sleep here.

00:41:08.926 --> 00:41:10.553
Wh-What are you doing?!

00:41:10.636 --> 00:41:13.013
I'm changing clothes.
Isn't it obvious?

00:41:13.097 --> 00:41:15.015
Oh, it's just...

00:41:15.099 --> 00:41:18.060
Can't you, uhh,
do it somewhere else...?

00:41:19.311 --> 00:41:22.356
What are you getting perturbed for?
You've no reason to--

00:41:22.439 --> 00:41:23.899
--Go hide somewhere.

00:41:23.899 --> 00:41:26.360
--Oh, r-right!
--Go hide somewhere.

00:41:26.443 --> 00:41:27.361
...Hurry UP!

00:41:27.361 --> 00:41:29.321
--Don't rush me...
--Hurry up!

00:41:31.365 --> 00:41:33.033
Do you have pajamas?

00:41:33.117 --> 00:41:34.201
Don't peek!

00:41:34.285 --> 00:41:35.995
I'm not!

00:41:36.078 --> 00:41:38.706
I'm asking if you have pajamas or not!

00:41:39.707 --> 00:41:42.459
I don't. I only have undergarments.

00:41:42.543 --> 00:41:46.338
Alastor cleanses my body with his flames,

00:41:46.422 --> 00:41:49.091
so I only change clothes
when I feel like it.

00:41:50.217 --> 00:41:53.262
So that "Hunter" guy at school today...

00:41:53.345 --> 00:41:55.556
He's the one making
all the Torches around town?

00:41:55.639 --> 00:41:57.433
A lot more than usual, too.

00:41:57.516 --> 00:42:02.563
Denizens don't normally eat
this many people in a single city.

00:42:02.646 --> 00:42:05.190
Torches are used to keep things in balance,

00:42:05.274 --> 00:42:09.486
but the more that are needed,
the more warped the world becomes.

00:42:09.570 --> 00:42:13.407
However, that could
very well be this Hunter's aim.

00:42:13.490 --> 00:42:14.533
His aim?

00:42:14.617 --> 00:42:19.204
The more Torches there are, the more
likely a Mystes like you will appear.

00:42:19.288 --> 00:42:23.167
It also makes it easy to
lure in Flame Hazes like us.

00:42:23.250 --> 00:42:25.252
These truly are hunting grounds.

00:42:25.336 --> 00:42:27.254
Yet, he acts too cocky

00:42:27.338 --> 00:42:31.091
for someone who can't tell
what Flame Hazes he'll attract.

00:42:31.175 --> 00:42:34.595
Indeed, too much play could prove fatal.

00:42:34.678 --> 00:42:37.681
Although this is a powerful
lord we're talking about.

00:42:37.765 --> 00:42:41.226
There must be a reason for his confidence.

00:42:41.310 --> 00:42:43.729
We'll find out what it is in battle.

00:42:43.812 --> 00:42:48.067
There's no school tomorrow,
so maybe we can leave town?

00:42:48.150 --> 00:42:50.527
I don't want to get more
people caught up in this again...

00:42:50.611 --> 00:42:54.239
Okay. But you're sticking with me.

00:42:54.323 --> 00:42:55.532
You're my bait, after all.

00:42:55.616 --> 00:42:57.576
Yeah. I know.

00:43:00.996 --> 00:43:02.373
Oww...

00:43:11.340 --> 00:43:14.301
Urgh! That deserved ten more punches!

00:43:14.385 --> 00:43:17.054
I don't understand you.
It's only a Torch.

00:43:17.137 --> 00:43:17.972
SQ?

00:43:18.055 --> 00:43:22.059
Would you feel embarrassment
disrobing in front of a tree or a rock?

00:43:22.142 --> 00:43:24.144
Normally, you wouldn't care.

00:43:24.228 --> 00:43:26.105
I just didn't like it, that's all!

00:43:26.188 --> 00:43:28.107
In other words, it's the first human

00:43:28.190 --> 00:43:31.527
you've come to associate
with in a long time?

00:43:31.610 --> 00:43:33.112
It's not human.

00:43:33.195 --> 00:43:36.198
It's just a Torch
that's about to burn out.

00:43:36.281 --> 00:43:37.658
Mm.

00:43:54.216 --> 00:43:57.136
No one suspects a thing, Marianne.

00:43:59.013 --> 00:44:02.641
Not even the renowned
Flame of the Heavens...

00:44:02.725 --> 00:44:05.686
Still, Master.

00:44:05.769 --> 00:44:11.066
There are more Flame Hazes
paying attention to this city now.

00:44:11.150 --> 00:44:12.943
Please be careful.

00:44:14.987 --> 00:44:17.448
Do not worry, Marianne.

00:44:17.531 --> 00:44:21.368
Soon we will have
gathered enough power for you.

00:44:23.620 --> 00:44:26.290
I won't let anyone interfere.

00:44:53.275 --> 00:44:56.236
How brightly these Torches shine.

00:44:56.320 --> 00:45:03.243
Once this plan succeeds,
you will cease to be a Rinne tool.

00:45:03.327 --> 00:45:06.997
You will become an actual being--
an inhabitant of this world.

00:45:11.418 --> 00:45:13.087
Master...

00:45:13.170 --> 00:45:16.423
You've already done so much for me.

00:45:21.428 --> 00:45:24.389
No, it's not yet enough.

00:45:28.560 --> 00:45:32.689
If it weren't for the power I give you,

00:45:32.773 --> 00:45:35.567
you would vanish in under three days.

00:45:37.820 --> 00:45:40.739
Far too fleeting of an existence.

00:45:40.823 --> 00:45:46.787
I see it as a bond we share--
one too difficult to put into words.

00:45:46.870 --> 00:45:51.458
Oh, Marianne. Your words bring me such joy.

00:45:53.794 --> 00:45:55.170
Still...

00:45:57.297 --> 00:46:00.676
This is something I must accomplish.

00:46:00.759 --> 00:46:03.428
My reason for coming
from the Crimson World...

00:46:03.512 --> 00:46:05.973
My reason for seeking
existences in this world...

00:46:08.559 --> 00:46:12.646
It was all for you, Marianne.

00:46:33.041 --> 00:46:38.547
Interesting. With this many Torches,
something's definitely up.

00:46:38.630 --> 00:46:41.633
This city stinks more than the rumors say.

00:46:41.717 --> 00:46:44.720
Yeah, it reeks all right...

00:46:44.803 --> 00:46:47.431
Of your boozy breath!

00:46:50.184 --> 00:46:52.895
Shut up, Stupid Marco.

00:46:52.978 --> 00:46:56.523
Oh? I sense a Flame Haze as well.

00:46:56.607 --> 00:46:59.526
Yeah. Guess someone else
beat us to the punch.

00:46:59.610 --> 00:47:01.653
Wanna move on?

00:47:01.737 --> 00:47:03.906
Now why would I do that?

00:47:03.989 --> 00:47:07.993
First to find, first to kill.
That's how it works.

00:47:09.620 --> 00:47:10.829
For sure!

00:47:10.913 --> 00:47:16.460
So let's do some slaughtering,
my beloved goblet, Margery Daw!

00:47:16.543 --> 00:47:17.920
Naturally!

00:47:37.439 --> 00:47:38.523
Alastor...

00:47:38.607 --> 00:47:41.026
Mm. A Flame Haze.

00:47:46.323 --> 00:47:50.953
The film crew has just entered a
region known as the "Yellow Band."

00:47:51.036 --> 00:47:55.290
We're currently in what's
regarded as the most grueling part

00:47:55.374 --> 00:47:58.043
of the climb up Mt. Everest...

00:48:01.838 --> 00:48:03.423
I just can't do it...

00:48:03.507 --> 00:48:06.551
I don't have enough courage
yet to give Sakai-kun cookies...

00:48:23.110 --> 00:48:26.238
I'll wait until I'm a little braver.

00:48:39.710 --> 00:48:42.754
Someday, I'll be able to tell him.

00:48:45.215 --> 00:48:46.800
Hurry UP!

00:48:46.883 --> 00:48:49.594
Okay! Just gimme a second!

00:48:53.056 --> 00:48:56.018
You're the one who said
you don't want to fight here--

00:49:02.149 --> 00:49:05.360
Did you see its flame, Alastor?

00:49:05.444 --> 00:49:06.611
Mm.

00:49:06.695 --> 00:49:10.157
The Treasure inside this Mystes...
Could it be?

00:49:30.969 --> 00:49:35.640
It's hard getting used to this,
seeing people's flames...

00:49:35.724 --> 00:49:38.685
It's like I'm peeking into their lifespans.

00:49:38.769 --> 00:49:41.563
They even beat like heartbeats...

00:49:43.565 --> 00:49:44.941
Heartbeats?

00:49:45.025 --> 00:49:46.485
How so?

00:49:47.319 --> 00:49:50.822
What do you mean?
You guys see it too, don't you?

00:49:50.906 --> 00:49:53.325
Everyone's flames
flickering and expanding...

00:49:54.785 --> 00:49:55.744
<i>Master!</i>

00:49:55.827 --> 00:49:58.330
No, I don't see it, either.

00:49:58.413 --> 00:50:01.083
Huh? But it's so clear...

00:50:07.964 --> 00:50:11.510
You really are a strange Mystes.

00:50:11.593 --> 00:50:14.638
I think it's because of the
Treasure inside you, though.

00:50:14.721 --> 00:50:16.098
Huh?

00:50:17.140 --> 00:50:20.394
It's most likely
something quite unusual.

00:50:20.477 --> 00:50:23.855
There's no way to know
without opening you up, though.

00:50:25.565 --> 00:50:28.026
More concerning, however,

00:50:28.110 --> 00:50:30.570
is this Torch "heartbeat"
of which you speak.

00:50:30.654 --> 00:50:32.447
What are other ones doing?

00:50:32.531 --> 00:50:35.700
As far as I can tell,
they're all beating.

00:50:35.784 --> 00:50:37.786
They don't usually do that.

00:50:37.869 --> 00:50:42.707
Or it could be that all the
Torches in this particular city do.

00:50:43.959 --> 00:50:45.085
Alastor...

00:50:45.168 --> 00:50:48.505
Mm. There may be
some sort of scheme at work...

00:50:55.595 --> 00:50:57.556
An Unrestricted Method!

00:51:10.277 --> 00:51:12.529
A search Method...

00:51:12.612 --> 00:51:14.739
Why did that person just disappear?

00:51:14.823 --> 00:51:18.827
Unrestricted Methods
require the power of existence.

00:51:18.910 --> 00:51:21.079
That Torch must've been used for that.

00:51:21.163 --> 00:51:23.832
You can't be serious!
Who'd do something like that?!

00:51:23.915 --> 00:51:25.167
Was it that Friagne guy?!

00:51:25.250 --> 00:51:30.547
No, it's the Flame Haze we've
been sensing since yesterday night.

00:51:30.630 --> 00:51:32.048
It appears they aren't backing off.

00:51:32.132 --> 00:51:34.968
Huh? There's another
Flame Haze besides Shana?

00:51:35.051 --> 00:51:37.179
Don't call me that!

00:51:37.929 --> 00:51:42.142
All these Torches here are
bound to attract Flame Hazes.

00:51:42.225 --> 00:51:44.853
They must intend to lure out the Hunter.

00:51:53.069 --> 00:51:55.113
Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John!

00:51:55.197 --> 00:52:00.160
Cover all corners and find
the ghost who disrupts our dreams!

00:52:14.132 --> 00:52:16.551
Master, the Torches...

00:52:16.635 --> 00:52:19.721
They can't possibly know yet...

00:52:19.804 --> 00:52:23.683
However, it looks like
we'll have to hurry, Marianne.

00:52:23.767 --> 00:52:25.018
It's just as you said;

00:52:25.101 --> 00:52:29.773
having so many Flame Hazes
coming to visit is becoming bothersome.

00:53:01.263 --> 00:53:03.098
Looks like they didn't fall for it.

00:53:03.181 --> 00:53:05.600
I dunno, if there's a Denizen nearby,

00:53:05.684 --> 00:53:09.688
won't they be like, "Crap, they found me!"
and then rush outta hiding?

00:53:09.771 --> 00:53:13.316
Looks like we've
netted something else, too.

00:53:15.068 --> 00:53:16.570
What do you think you're doing?!

00:53:16.653 --> 00:53:19.864
Oh, my. How uncouth.

00:53:19.948 --> 00:53:21.783
Not even a "hello"?

00:53:21.866 --> 00:53:25.203
"Chanter of Elegies"
and "Claws and Fangs of Violation"...

00:53:25.287 --> 00:53:26.997
So it was you two...

00:53:27.080 --> 00:53:30.667
Yo, yo, yo! If it ain't
Flame of the Heavens!

00:53:30.750 --> 00:53:34.921
Which means you must
be Flame-haired Burning-eyed.

00:53:35.005 --> 00:53:37.924
What a tiny, little child.

00:53:38.008 --> 00:53:40.969
Just what are you doing here?

00:53:53.356 --> 00:53:55.775
Are you the ones who did it?!

00:53:55.859 --> 00:53:57.235
Huh?

00:53:58.028 --> 00:53:59.946
It was you, wasn't it?!

00:54:00.030 --> 00:54:01.489
HOW?!

00:54:01.573 --> 00:54:04.784
How can you extinguish
Torches so easily?!

00:54:04.868 --> 00:54:06.953
Huh? What is this?

00:54:07.037 --> 00:54:08.955
Looks like a Torch, but...

00:54:09.039 --> 00:54:14.294
Those Torches... they might've
had hopes and wants of their own!

00:54:14.377 --> 00:54:17.255
They might've had feelings!

00:54:23.303 --> 00:54:24.846
Why...?

00:54:24.929 --> 00:54:26.306
Why?!

00:54:35.815 --> 00:54:38.068
What's your deal?
You're annoying.

00:54:38.151 --> 00:54:40.779
Put it out!
Put out that annoying Torch!

00:54:40.862 --> 00:54:42.989
Wait! That's a Mystes!

00:54:43.073 --> 00:54:45.033
It must not be
destroyed haphazardly!

00:54:46.117 --> 00:54:48.995
You serious?! No wonder
it howls so much!

00:54:49.079 --> 00:54:50.664
Dammit...

00:54:50.747 --> 00:54:53.708
lam not taking sides with
the Mystes here,

00:54:53.792 --> 00:54:56.419
but I cannot say I approve of your
wanton extinguishing of Torches.

00:54:56.503 --> 00:54:59.381
A Flame Haze is supposed
to preserve balance!

00:54:59.464 --> 00:55:02.300
What carefree nonsense.

00:55:02.384 --> 00:55:06.805
With so many Torches already, leaving
things alone seems crazier to me.

00:55:06.888 --> 00:55:09.849
You're slackin' off, Flamer!

00:55:09.933 --> 00:55:12.852
I am aware of the excessive
number of Torches.

00:55:12.936 --> 00:55:17.440
However, it appears they
have been rigged in some manner.

00:55:17.524 --> 00:55:18.900
Rigged?

00:55:20.777 --> 00:55:24.364
Then this could be a
trap to kill Flame Hazes.

00:55:24.447 --> 00:55:26.324
I'm sure you've heard

00:55:26.408 --> 00:55:29.786
that many of our peers have
gone missing around here.

00:55:31.121 --> 00:55:35.208
That's why we superstars
have rolled into town!

00:55:35.291 --> 00:55:39.087
We've found the sheer number
of Torches here to be most curious.

00:55:39.170 --> 00:55:42.382
Yeah, it shocked us too
when we first came to town.

00:55:42.465 --> 00:55:45.135
Definitely ain't normal...

00:55:45.218 --> 00:55:47.178
Rigged for something, huh...

00:55:55.478 --> 00:55:58.398
Alastor. I sense something bad.

00:55:58.481 --> 00:55:59.232
Mm.

00:56:06.322 --> 00:56:10.994
A Flame Haze gossip session...
What a rare sight.

00:56:13.329 --> 00:56:14.247
Friagne!

00:56:14.330 --> 00:56:17.417
Well, well, well.
It's the big shot himself.

00:56:17.500 --> 00:56:18.752
The Hunter, huh?

00:56:18.835 --> 00:56:21.379
Oh, man! This is sweet!

00:56:21.463 --> 00:56:23.256
You must be Chanter of Elegies

00:56:23.339 --> 00:56:26.342
and Claws and Fangs of Violation.

00:56:26.426 --> 00:56:29.137
That explains the
boorish Unrestricted Methods.

00:56:29.220 --> 00:56:32.932
You went and ruined
the city-wide painting I made.

00:56:33.016 --> 00:56:35.268
I feel just awful.

00:56:35.351 --> 00:56:38.855
And there's plenty
more where that came from!

00:56:38.938 --> 00:56:40.315
Seal!

00:56:47.280 --> 00:56:49.032
Hunter Friagne!

00:56:49.115 --> 00:56:52.076
Say your prayers!

00:57:01.336 --> 00:57:03.379
A city-wide painting...?!

00:57:06.883 --> 00:57:08.843
Too slow!

00:57:18.561 --> 00:57:19.521
The flames...!

00:57:19.604 --> 00:57:21.189
How did you...?!

00:57:21.898 --> 00:57:24.984
The Azure, my fire-repelling ring.

00:57:25.068 --> 00:57:30.281
A beautiful, dignified Treasure that
wards away all manners of flame.

00:57:30.365 --> 00:57:34.994
Hah! What is it about collectors that
makes them such big show-offs?!

00:57:35.078 --> 00:57:37.539
And always lame, at that!

00:57:37.622 --> 00:57:39.457
I'm sorry to hear that.

00:57:39.541 --> 00:57:41.125
In that case...

00:57:45.672 --> 00:57:47.632
Maybe you'll like this.

00:57:53.304 --> 00:57:54.764
The Bubble Root...

00:57:54.848 --> 00:57:58.017
One of my most prized Treasures.

00:57:58.101 --> 00:58:02.772
There's not a single weapon
that can cut through it.

00:58:04.649 --> 00:58:08.319
Then this calls for an
up-close-and-personal beat-down!

00:58:18.037 --> 00:58:21.875
Damn! I forgot he's an
expert at playing with dolls!

00:58:37.140 --> 00:58:40.101
If I can't cut this,
then I'll cut its owner!

00:58:49.110 --> 00:58:51.070
Stupid little toys!

00:58:53.573 --> 00:58:54.949
That's...!

00:58:59.454 --> 00:59:01.039
Get back!

00:59:11.716 --> 00:59:15.428
Damn. Any closer and she
woulda been blown to smithereens!

00:59:15.511 --> 00:59:17.472
That Mystes...

00:59:27.398 --> 00:59:31.444
It somehow saw through
my Dance Party's explosions...

00:59:31.527 --> 00:59:34.489
Was it the power of the Treasure inside it?

00:59:48.544 --> 00:59:50.797
You're a bit of an eyesore.

01:00:12.944 --> 01:00:16.572
Amusing! A Flame Haze,
stopping her sword mid-swing!

01:00:21.202 --> 01:00:23.538
I'll be taking this now.

01:00:26.082 --> 01:00:27.291
Get the hell back here!

01:00:27.375 --> 01:00:28.668
Flame Hazes.

01:00:28.751 --> 01:00:31.004
If you still wish to fight,

01:00:31.087 --> 01:00:35.008
then come to the highest
point in the city tonight.

01:00:35.091 --> 01:00:38.511
I'll have the perfect stage
ready and waiting for you.

01:00:53.776 --> 01:00:56.571
Ugh. He got away.

01:00:56.654 --> 01:00:59.282
Sheesh. What were you thinking?

01:01:08.624 --> 01:01:10.460
Why did l...:>!

01:01:13.880 --> 01:01:18.468
It appears the Flame Hazes
won't be trouble for much longer.

01:01:18.551 --> 01:01:20.344
Thanks to that.

01:01:23.347 --> 01:01:27.226
And, once we've eliminated them...

01:01:28.478 --> 01:01:32.231
Marianne. You will be reborn.

01:01:32.315 --> 01:01:37.153
You will become a single,
distinct, and self-reliant being.

01:01:37.236 --> 01:01:41.157
Once that happens, eternity will be ours.

01:01:41.240 --> 01:01:42.617
Master...

01:01:44.744 --> 01:01:46.662
Eternity...?

01:01:46.746 --> 01:01:51.667
You mean he didn't make all
those Torches to collect Treasures?!

01:01:51.751 --> 01:01:55.004
Damn! I can't just sit here like this...!

01:02:09.060 --> 01:02:12.146
Why did l...?

01:02:15.566 --> 01:02:18.945
That's what it is to
become involved with someone.

01:02:24.826 --> 01:02:26.410
Involved with...

01:02:30.706 --> 01:02:33.417
Damn, take it easy!

01:02:33.501 --> 01:02:35.711
You plannin' to fight drunk or something?

01:02:35.795 --> 01:02:40.216
Gimme a break. My search
Methods don't have any effect.

01:02:40.299 --> 01:02:44.095
All we can do is
wait until night like he wants.

01:02:49.475 --> 01:02:53.187
You can just cleanse the
booze out when it's time to go.

01:02:53.271 --> 01:02:56.816
Geez! My cleansing flame
ain't for sobering up, y'know!

01:03:06.659 --> 01:03:08.870
That Torch I've gotten involved with...

01:03:08.953 --> 01:03:10.663
I'm not throwing it away.

01:03:10.746 --> 01:03:12.707
I'm putting it to use!

01:03:18.629 --> 01:03:22.717
Hey. Quit spacing out, will you?

01:03:22.800 --> 01:03:24.385
This is seriously annoying.

01:03:24.468 --> 01:03:27.305
Having my time wasted
because you screwed up...

01:03:27.388 --> 01:03:30.183
Not like you got
any other plans, though!

01:03:32.935 --> 01:03:36.355
If you're just gonna get
in the way, then don't come.

01:03:37.899 --> 01:03:38.774
--I'm going!

01:03:38.774 --> 01:03:40.151
"Huh?
"I'm going!

01:03:40.902 --> 01:03:41.944
--I'm going to fight!

01:03:41.944 --> 01:03:43.821
--You don't say...
--I'm going to fight!

01:03:46.657 --> 01:03:49.911
Finally got that Flame Haze
look back, huh?!

01:03:49.994 --> 01:03:52.455
This is gonna be one hell of a night!

01:03:52.538 --> 01:03:54.540
Right, Flamer?!

01:04:23.694 --> 01:04:24.695
What do you think?

01:04:24.779 --> 01:04:27.448
A magnificent stage, wouldn't you say?

01:04:27.531 --> 01:04:30.201
Now we simply wait for the Flame Hazes.

01:04:47.093 --> 01:04:49.011
Observe, Mystes.

01:04:49.095 --> 01:04:51.305
This is known as the Trigger Happy.

01:04:51.389 --> 01:04:54.642
It's a weapon meant
for killing Flame Hazes.

01:04:56.560 --> 01:05:02.191
Flame Hazes use their bodies
as vessels to harbor Crimson Lords.

01:05:02.275 --> 01:05:06.654
Flame-haired Burning-eyed harbors
Alastor, Flame of the Heavens, for instance.

01:05:09.365 --> 01:05:12.827
However, a Lord's power is immense.

01:05:12.910 --> 01:05:17.290
So a Lord's existence
must be made dormant

01:05:17.373 --> 01:05:19.292
before entering a Flame Haze vessel.

01:05:19.375 --> 01:05:22.044
But this Trigger Happy here...

01:05:25.589 --> 01:05:28.467
...can end a Lord's dormancy.

01:05:33.931 --> 01:05:36.434
The enormous power of
an awakened Lord

01:05:36.517 --> 01:05:39.854
will instantaneously destroy
its Flame Haze vessel.

01:05:39.937 --> 01:05:43.983
In short, the Flame Haze
ends up exploding.

01:05:44.066 --> 01:05:45.484
Doesn't that sound fun?

01:05:45.568 --> 01:05:49.405
What's more, the Lord will so
fear disrupting this world's balance

01:05:49.488 --> 01:05:51.365
that it must simply return
to the Crimson World.

01:05:51.449 --> 01:05:55.786
That leaves only the victor
remaining... Me, in other words.

01:05:55.870 --> 01:05:58.914
So not even the Flame of
the Heavens' appearance here

01:05:58.998 --> 01:06:01.667
will bring harm to the city.

01:06:01.751 --> 01:06:04.795
Marianne. This will
be a magnificent show.

01:06:04.879 --> 01:06:07.631
Yes, Master.

01:06:07.715 --> 01:06:11.510
Why would he bother
to worry about the city?

01:06:11.594 --> 01:06:15.556
It shouldn't matter to
them if it gets destroyed or not...

01:06:39.330 --> 01:06:40.873
--Shall we go?

01:06:40.873 --> 01:06:42.458
--Mm.
--Shall we go?

01:06:44.460 --> 01:06:46.462
It's time to go all out, Marcosias!

01:06:46.545 --> 01:06:48.339
Let's do it!

01:07:29.505 --> 01:07:31.882
Don't let him shoot you!

01:07:38.931 --> 01:07:39.932
The Trigger Happy?

01:07:40.015 --> 01:07:43.144
Damn! That's his trump card?!

01:07:44.812 --> 01:07:45.604
--Be careful!

01:07:45.604 --> 01:07:46.981
--Yeah!
--Be careful!

01:07:54.196 --> 01:07:58.451
Flame Haze. I'll blow
you away in a single go.

01:08:20.723 --> 01:08:22.099
Shana!

01:08:36.530 --> 01:08:39.742
Flame Hazes, fighting side-by-side...

01:08:39.825 --> 01:08:41.785
Today is special!

01:09:02.223 --> 01:09:05.142
The Torch-beats are getting bigger...

01:09:05.226 --> 01:09:07.895
Something strange is definitely going on!

01:09:14.360 --> 01:09:17.154
Shana! He's not trying to hunt!

01:09:17.238 --> 01:09:20.032
He's got the entire
city rigged for something!

01:09:57.319 --> 01:09:58.737
What is this?

01:09:58.821 --> 01:10:01.991
Rigged Torches,
throughout the entire city...

01:10:02.074 --> 01:10:03.534
Could it be?!

01:10:04.159 --> 01:10:05.703
Hunter Friagne!

01:10:05.786 --> 01:10:09.081
Is the "City Devouring" your goal?!

01:10:09.164 --> 01:10:10.416
“Say What?!

01:10:10.416 --> 01:10:12.501
“CRY Devourins?!
“SaY What?!

01:10:12.585 --> 01:10:15.337
It's too late to do anything now.

01:10:15.421 --> 01:10:18.090
That's right, the infamous City Devouring,

01:10:18.173 --> 01:10:20.551
once achieved by a Crimson Lord.

01:10:24.179 --> 01:10:28.851
The transformation of an entire
city into a giant bundle of power...

01:10:36.442 --> 01:10:38.152
I can do it.

01:10:38.235 --> 01:10:41.030
No, I am doing it.

01:10:41.113 --> 01:10:43.657
I won't allow you to interfere.

01:10:54.376 --> 01:10:56.962
He's turning the city into energy...?

01:10:57.046 --> 01:11:01.008
Then this city, Mom,
and everyone else are...!

01:11:08.098 --> 01:11:11.101
The City Devouring?!
It's time we get serious, partner!

01:11:11.185 --> 01:11:14.229
I know! But how do we stop it?!

01:11:14.313 --> 01:11:16.899
We'll just hafta slaughter the Hunter!

01:11:16.982 --> 01:11:19.985
Hurry! The world will collapse
if the City Devouring takes place!

01:11:20.069 --> 01:11:21.445
Right!

01:11:44.385 --> 01:11:45.761
That bell...

01:11:45.844 --> 01:11:48.806
Sometimes it makes explosions,
and sometimes it doesn't...

01:11:53.519 --> 01:11:54.311
That's it!

01:11:54.395 --> 01:11:56.355
He acts like he's attacking,

01:11:56.438 --> 01:11:59.400
but the bell is actually
causing the City Devouring!

01:12:09.451 --> 01:12:11.203
I have to tell them...

01:12:11.286 --> 01:12:13.372
I'm the only one who knows!

01:12:13.455 --> 01:12:15.207
There's still a way to stop him...

01:12:15.290 --> 01:12:18.335
There's still a way to save the city...!

01:12:19.878 --> 01:12:23.006
This is something only I can do now!

01:12:42.818 --> 01:12:46.363
And I had hoped to end
this with one shot from this gun...

01:12:48.824 --> 01:12:51.452
They're tougher than I thought.

01:12:58.667 --> 01:13:01.628
Master. Allow me.

01:13:01.712 --> 01:13:04.465
No, Marianne. The time is near.

01:13:07.801 --> 01:13:09.470
Master.

01:13:09.553 --> 01:13:14.767
Life will be too unbearable
for me if these people slay you.

01:13:14.850 --> 01:13:18.145
But... the opposite isn't true.

01:13:20.856 --> 01:13:24.276
Please, Master.

01:13:24.359 --> 01:13:28.280
You're all that matters to me...

01:13:28.363 --> 01:13:31.283
You're all that matters to me...!

01:13:54.264 --> 01:13:56.141
Master! Hurry!

01:14:00.145 --> 01:14:02.105
Master Friagne...

01:14:39.184 --> 01:14:41.103
Marianne...

01:14:41.186 --> 01:14:42.563
Yes...

01:14:43.772 --> 01:14:48.193
<i>I will</i> revive you...

01:14:48.277 --> 01:14:53.866
And then we'll live together, forever...

01:14:53.949 --> 01:14:56.869
Just one more ring...
Two more rings...

01:14:56.952 --> 01:14:59.830
And the City Devouring will be complete...

01:15:05.377 --> 01:15:06.753
But first...

01:15:07.963 --> 01:15:09.840
You must die!

01:15:11.133 --> 01:15:12.926
Not good...

01:15:14.052 --> 01:15:17.598
You... pathetic Tool
for Destruction Attack!

01:15:17.681 --> 01:15:19.474
Make a Seal!

01:15:34.489 --> 01:15:36.909
The City Devouring stopped...

01:16:04.227 --> 01:16:05.938
Destroy it all!

01:16:06.021 --> 01:16:08.106
Everything! Everything!

01:16:08.190 --> 01:16:09.983
Everything!

01:16:13.028 --> 01:16:13.654
Shana!

01:16:13.695 --> 01:16:15.155
Little brat!

01:16:22.204 --> 01:16:23.580
What?!

01:16:27.250 --> 01:16:28.377
Hey! Is this...?!

01:16:28.460 --> 01:16:30.253
It can't be!

01:16:46.603 --> 01:16:49.147
Crap! That's Flame of the Heavens!

01:16:49.231 --> 01:16:51.316
Run, before we get caught in it!

01:16:51.400 --> 01:16:52.985
Screw this!

01:16:53.527 --> 01:16:55.112
Hurry, Marcosias!

01:17:19.594 --> 01:17:21.513
<i>Th-That's...</i>

01:17:21.596 --> 01:17:23.473
...Flame of the Heavens...

01:17:23.557 --> 01:17:24.683
He's manifested...

01:17:24.766 --> 01:17:27.602
The God of Atonement has
actually manifested in this world...

01:17:27.686 --> 01:17:31.023
But how? He was
hit by the Trigger Happy...

01:17:32.441 --> 01:17:35.193
Hunter Friagne...

01:17:35.277 --> 01:17:36.737
Such foolishness...

01:17:38.196 --> 01:17:41.158
Flame of the Heavens...

01:17:44.286 --> 01:17:47.372
This little one will not explode.

01:17:47.456 --> 01:17:54.254
Truly powerful is the owner
of a vessel that can contain me.

01:18:03.555 --> 01:18:07.059
Did you sincerely believe
that I, a Crimson God,

01:18:07.142 --> 01:18:10.395
would make a contract with just anyone?

01:18:12.022 --> 01:18:13.815
Now accept this...!

01:18:15.901 --> 01:18:18.862
The Fire of Retribution!

01:18:24.367 --> 01:18:26.787
Mari...anne...

01:19:16.211 --> 01:19:17.587
Hey...

01:19:21.633 --> 01:19:24.094
Do I have enough to fix this?

01:19:25.929 --> 01:19:29.182
At this point, you've
not even an ember left.

01:19:29.266 --> 01:19:32.227
You're no more than a spark now...

01:19:34.855 --> 01:19:36.231
Oh...

01:19:39.901 --> 01:19:41.903
It's strange.

01:19:41.987 --> 01:19:44.698
I'm sad I'm going to disappear...

01:19:44.781 --> 01:19:48.326
But it doesn't bother me anymore.

01:19:48.410 --> 01:19:50.328
I understand now.

01:19:50.412 --> 01:19:53.582
It doesn't matter who or what you are.

01:19:53.665 --> 01:19:56.209
It's all about doing what you can now.

01:19:56.293 --> 01:19:58.253
That's all that matters...

01:20:00.547 --> 01:20:02.424
You worry about silly things.

01:20:02.507 --> 01:20:03.675
Yeah...

01:20:03.758 --> 01:20:06.469
You always did.

01:20:06.553 --> 01:20:08.430
Did I?

01:20:08.513 --> 01:20:11.057
Yeah, I guess I did...

01:20:12.976 --> 01:20:15.395
Shana“.

01:20:15.478 --> 01:20:16.897
I have a favor to ask...

01:20:16.980 --> 01:20:18.773
What is it?

01:20:19.566 --> 01:20:21.860
The name "Shana"...

01:20:21.943 --> 01:20:23.904
Could you keep on using it?

01:20:25.947 --> 01:20:27.324
Sure.

01:20:51.765 --> 01:20:53.558
Huh?! Wham?!

01:20:53.642 --> 01:20:57.854
I'm here... I'm still here!
I haven't disappeared!

01:20:57.938 --> 01:20:59.898
This can't be real!

01:20:59.981 --> 01:21:01.358
How...?

01:21:05.904 --> 01:21:07.614
Yuji Sakai.

01:21:07.697 --> 01:21:12.535
<i>This</i> is the power of the Treasure inside you.

01:21:12.619 --> 01:21:16.915
At each stroke of midnight,
it restores your power of existence.

01:21:16.998 --> 01:21:20.418
The Treasure is known
as the "Midnight Lost Child."

01:21:20.502 --> 01:21:21.461
--Then...?

01:21:21.461 --> 01:21:23.755
--That's right. You won't disappear.
--Then...?

01:21:23.838 --> 01:21:28.426
However, the fact remains
that you are an imperiled Mystes.

01:21:28.510 --> 01:21:32.722
We will stay here and continue
to watch over you for a while.

01:21:32.806 --> 01:21:34.683
O-Okay!

01:21:37.894 --> 01:21:39.521
Any problems with that?

01:21:39.604 --> 01:21:41.022
Nope.

01:21:41.106 --> 01:21:42.482
Good.

01:22:25.984 --> 01:22:35.118
<i>A blade that silently pierces
the darkness screams out</i>

01:22:35.201 --> 01:22:42.542
<i>and eyes bearing
bright red flames pulsate</i>

01:22:42.625 --> 01:22:47.756
<i>At some point,
an all-enveloping blaze</i>

01:22:47.839 --> 01:22:51.926
<i>has chosen both path and destiny</i>

01:22:52.010 --> 01:22:59.184
<i>I glance down at
a small, flickering light</i>

01:22:59.267 --> 01:23:08.068
<i>and feel the warmth of a quick breath</i>

01:23:08.151 --> 01:23:12.072
<i>I feel it now</i>

01:23:12.155 --> 01:23:22.665
<i>This is what it means to "exist"</i>

01:23:22.749 --> 01:23:31.257
<i>Your solitary time on heaven
and earth is shattered</i>

01:23:31.341 --> 01:23:39.140
<i>as a new encounter knocks
on the door of your closed heart</i>

01:23:39.224 --> 01:23:47.857
<i>A truth I can't tell you can't
transform into your tears</i>

01:23:47.941 --> 01:23:54.197
<i>So I want to find new courage</i>

01:23:54.280 --> 01:24:00.036
<i>at the end of the burning sky</i>

01:24:18.596 --> 01:24:27.897
<i>I'm sure tomorrow will be the same--
people who are intimate</i>

01:24:27.981 --> 01:24:35.155
<i>will continue on as always,
deaf to the voice of life</i>

01:24:35.238 --> 01:24:40.452
<i>At some point you nestled up to me</i>

01:24:40.535 --> 01:24:44.456
<i>with an all-knowing smile</i>

01:24:44.539 --> 01:24:51.713
<i>[pretended not to
care and turned</i> away

01:24:51.796 --> 01:25:00.346
<i>to which you let out a sad sigh</i>

01:25:00.430 --> 01:25:05.059
<i>I now feel in my heart</i>

01:25:05.143 --> 01:25:15.236
<i>that this is "love"</i>

01:25:15.320 --> 01:25:23.912
<i>Now that you've been released by
the heavens' solitude, I embrace you</i>

01:25:23.995 --> 01:25:32.086
<i>while your tiny shoulders
tremble like droplets</i>

01:25:32.170 --> 01:25:40.678
<i>And as reality pierces you,
the sword of your heart strikes back</i>

01:25:40.762 --> 01:25:47.018
<i>I want to find unyielding courage,</i>

01:25:47.101 --> 01:25:52.857
<i>like the powerful wind</i>
